["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"entity-runtime","stream_identity":"01a0cab7-1ed7-77a5-8384-ff10c92e7ad6","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"aep.entity","fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"MIG8ecf045456184e7359987fe90844d1cccbb924fc2e68a33f644a918d462e685f","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/validated-definition-boundary","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":5,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"## Context\n\nPublic free functions currently accept raw definitions, while default handling, duplicate YAML keys, nested paths and single-file CLI validation leave routes around registration.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nEvery create, execute and replay entry point requires a `ValidatedDefinition`, and registration reports every independent defect across schemas, defaults, rules, templates and projections before storing nothing on refusal.\n\n## Implementation evidence\n\nMoved to implemented on 2026-09-09 after an audit of every non-implemented artifact against `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/roadmap.md` and the crates.\n\nKernel entry points take only `ValidatedDefinition` (`crates/entity-core/src/registry.rs`); registration accumulates every independent defect and stores nothing on refusal (`DefinitionErrors`).\n","relations":[{"decomposes":"epic:kernel"},{"serves":"vision:O2"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"Registration accumulates every definition defect and produces the sole handle accepted by kernel entry points.","title":"Only validated definitions reach execution"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"}},"id":"MIG8ecf045456184e7359987fe90844d1cccbb924fc2e68a33f644a918d462e685f","lifecycle_state":"recorded","revision":5,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["aep.entity","MIG8ecf045456184e7359987fe90844d1cccbb924fc2e68a33f644a918d462e685f"]}]